From 21ded065fe4a6c09e4e2be77c63949dac2999282 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 06:07:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(contests): mode picker (QCM vs solve-on-paper + photo) +
 official subject link
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Tapping a contest now opens a bottom sheet: 'QCM interactif' (existing
  flow, unchanged) or 'Résoudre sur papier' (new)
- New ContestPhotoSubmissionScreen: links out to the official subject
  archive (concours-ingenieurs.rnu.tn/epreuves, the DGET/MESRS portal
  for the Tunisian national engineering entrance exams, deep-linked by
  année), lets the student photograph their paper-solved work (camera
  or gallery via image_picker), and submits it via the new backend
  endpoint. Shows a 'pending review' status once submitted.
- Added image_picker + url_launcher deps, camera/photo-library usage
  strings in Info.plist, CAMERA permission in AndroidManifest.xml
- Explicitly out of scope here (per request): reviewing/grading the
  submitted photos — that's a separate admin-side workflow
